Add the settings module of the KDecoration3 window decoration

The KDecoration3 decoration reads the kwinqtcurverc file of the KDE4
decoration, and its plugin metadata names no configuration module. The pencil
button of System Settings > Window Decorations therefore opens nothing. Only
the settings dialogue of the QtCurve style writes the file today.

The commit adds qt6/kdecoration/config, a KCMUtils plugin with the name
kcm_qtcurvedecoration. kcoreaddons_add_plugin() installs it in the
org.kde.kdecoration3.kcm directory of the Qt plugin path, and
kcmutils_generate_desktop_file() adds its desktop file. qtcurve.json gains
X-KDE-ConfigModule, so KWin opens the module from the pencil button.

The module edits the keys of the kwinqtcurverc file that change the decoration.
The General group holds OuterBorder, InnerBorder, RoundBottom, CustomShadows,
TitleBarPad and EdgePad. The two shadow groups hold Size, HOffset, VOffset,
ColorType and Color. The module writes Color for the CT_CUSTOM colour type
alone, and it removes the key for every other type. It keeps every other key,
and it edits no key of the file of the style. The colour buttons show the
colour of the current type, and the custom shadow box drives them.

Warning: the KWin page of the style writes the same file, and the last save
wins. load() reads the file again before it fills the widgets.

save() sends the reloadConfig signal of org.kde.KWin, so the page needs no
restart of the compositor. Every decoration gets the reconfigured signal of
KDecoration3. DecorationConfig gains a generation counter, so the first
decoration of a signal does the read and the two shadow resets alone.

Out of scope: the BorderSize key, the two opacities, the opaque border and the
window grouping, which the decoration never reads.

The change sits on the branch work/kdecoration3 of the local tree, as the second
commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !9 on
system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

